 "notes": "Second read 2026-10-27: the parse kept all 30 rows but no places (the sheet prints none: two 'Top 15' tables, girls left and boys right, each in finish order), so places 1-15 are the list positions (girls 14/15 Moulin and Haeuser both 10:47, boys 5/6 Griffin and Talbot both 8:27, listed in that order). Names split over two cells ('Erica' / 'Jesseman') rejoined; TA = Thornton Academy, SP = South Portland (kept as printed; both are teams in the sheet's team list). The sheet prints no leg distance (SMAA Relays legs; later years 1.5-1.65 miles), so the events keep none. Not entered: the two team total-time columns under the lists (relay totals in h:mm:ss, e.g. Scarborough 51:55:00 girls, Scarborough 60:02:00 boys; not points) and the full leg grid, which is in smaarelayscomplete (relay legs, no place). Date: the sub5 index has September 1, 2005. | Third read 2026-10-28 (leftover check): the 30 rows re-compared to the source; all agree. The 27 'implausible' flags came only from the missing distance (relay-leg times read as a 5K). Event distance set to 1.55 Mile, the leg length of the same SMAA Relays series in 2009 (1.55 Mile from the MileSplit copy) and 2006: top-15 times here (boys best 8:03, median 8:31; girls best 9:14, median 10:29) match 2009 (boys 7:43 / 8:20; girls 8:53 / 9:59) and 2006 (boys 8:00 / 8:25; girls 8:47 / 10:00) within the usual spread. 2026-10-28 orchestrator: leg distance NOT set: the SMAA relay leg changed most years (2009 1.55, 2012 1.6, 2013 1.65, 2014-16 1.54, 2017 1.5, 2019 1.77 Mile), so 2009's length is no evidence for this year; the event stays without a distance."
